.TH "CHARACTERDATA.AFTER" "3JS" "October 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CharacterData.after \- CharacterData: after() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]after()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R]
interface inserts a set of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects or strings in the
children list of the \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R]\(cqs parent, just after
the \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R].
Strings are inserted as equivalent \f[CR]Text\f[R] nodes.
Nothing happens if \f[CR]parentNode\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
after(param1)
after(param1, param2)
after(param1, param2, /* \&..., */ paramN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]param1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]paramN\f[R]
A set of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects or strings to insert.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]HierarchyRequestError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown when the new nodes cannot be inserted at the specified point in
the hierarchy, that is if one of the following conditions is met:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
If the insertion of one of the added node would lead to a cycle, that is
if one of them is an ancestor of this \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] node.
.IP \(bu 2
If one of the added node is not a \f[CR]DocumentFragment\f[R], a
\f[CR]DocumentType\f[R], an \f[CR]Element\f[R], or a
\f[CR]CharacterData\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
If this \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] node is actually a \f[CR]Text\f[R]
node, and its parent is a \f[CR]Document\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
If the parent of this \f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] node is a
\f[CR]Document\f[R] and one of the nodes to insert is a
\f[CR]DocumentFragment\f[R] with more than one \f[CR]Element\f[R] child,
or that has a \f[CR]Text\f[R] child.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
The \f[CR]after()\f[R] method allows you to insert new nodes after a
\f[CR]CharacterData\f[R] node.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] h1TextNode = document.querySelector(\(dqh1\(dq).firstChild;
h1TextNode.after(\(dq #h1\(dq);

h1TextNode.parentElement.childNodes;
\f[I]// NodeList [#text \(dqCharacterData.after()\(dq, #text \(dq #h1\(dq]\f[R]

h1TextNode.data;
\f[I]// \(dqCharacterData.after()\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] If you rather want to append text to the current node,
the \f[CR]appendData()\f[R] method lets you append to the current
node\(cqs data.
.RE
